Now let $L=\frac{\dot q_1^{\,2}+\dot q_2^{\,2}}{2}
    -V(Aq_1+Bq_2),$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants. Then $\begin{aligned}
  \dot p_1&=-A\,V'(Aq_1+Bq_2),
  \notag\\
  \dot p_2&=-B\,V'(Aq_1+Bq_2).
  \end{aligned}$ Multiplying the first equation by $B$, the second by $A$, and subtracting eliminates the force: $\frac{d}{dt}(Bp_1-Ap_2)=0.$

